{"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/DateProtocol","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper"],"kind":"relationships"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"symbolKind":"class","externalID":"s:4GLib4DateC","title":"Date","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Date","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Date"}],"roleHeading":"Class"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Date","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GDate"},{"type":"text","text":" data structure represents a day between January 1, Year 1,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and sometime a few thousand years in the future (right now it will go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the year 65535 or so, but [method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.Date.set_parse"},{"text":"] only parses up to the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"year 8000 or so - just count on “a few thousand”). ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GDate"},{"type":"text","text":" is meant to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represent everyday dates, not astronomical dates or historical dates"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"or ISO timestamps or the like. It extrapolates the current Gregorian"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"calendar forward and backward in time; there is no attempt to change"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the calendar to match time periods or locations. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GDate"},{"type":"text","text":" does not store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time information; it represents a day."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"GDate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" implementation has several nice features; it is only a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"64-bit struct, so storing large numbers of dates is very efficient. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can keep both a Julian and day-month-year representation of the date,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"since some calculations are much easier with one representation or the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other. A Julian representation is simply a count of days since some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fixed day in the past; for "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Date"},{"text":" the fixed day is January 1, 1 AD.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(“Julian” dates in the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Date","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" API aren’t really Julian dates in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"technical sense; technically, Julian dates count from the start of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Julian period, Jan 1, 4713 BC).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"GDate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is simple to use. First you need a “blank” date; you can get a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"dynamically allocated date from [ctor"},{"code":"GLib.Date.new","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"], or you can declare an"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automatic variable or array and initialize it by calling [method","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.Date.clear","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A cleared date is safe; it’s safe to call [method","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.Date.set_dmy"},{"text":"] and the other","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"mutator functions to initialize the value of a cleared date. However, a cleared date","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is initially invalid, meaning that it doesn’t represent a day that exists."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"It is undefined to call any of the date calculation routines on an invalid date."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If you obtain a date from a user or other unpredictable source, you should check"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its validity with the [method"},{"code":"GLib.Date.valid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] predicate. [method","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.Date.valid"},{"type":"text","text":"]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"is also used to check for errors with [method","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.Date.set_parse"},{"type":"text","text":"] and other functions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that can fail. Dates can be invalidated by calling [method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.Date.clear"},{"type":"text","text":"] again."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is very important to use the API to access the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GDate"},{"type":"text","text":" struct. Often only the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"day-month-year or only the Julian representation is valid. Sometimes neither is valid.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Use the API."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"GLib also features ","type":"text"},{"code":"GDateTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" which represents a precise time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Date","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" type acts as an owner of an underlying ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GDate"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It provides the methods that can operate on this data type through "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/DateProtocol","isActive":true},{"text":" conformance.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Date","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" as a strong reference or owner of a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GDate"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/DateRef","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (instead of "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Date","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") for a lightweight Swift reference to an underlying "},{"code":"GDate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GDate"},{"type":"text","text":" is a struct for calendrical calculations."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Date\/init()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Date\/init(_:)-1xuni","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Date\/init(_:)-46imp","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Date\/init(_:)-4ld1t","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Date\/init(_:)-6bawz","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Date\/init(_:)-827x2","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Date\/init